   "summary": "The Foreign Office treats 1930–34 as the baseline set by the Far Eastern Commission, then reviews Japanese income, consumption, production, trade and international living-standard comparisons. It estimates that population growth would require higher national income, industrial output and imports and exports by 1953. It anticipates a larger role for machinery, metal and chemical industries and argues that wartime damage to housing, shipping and productive capacity would require further resources. The section includes the report’s cover, contents, main text and the first annexed price and industrial-output tables and diagram.",
